WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.835
A strong OSINT workflow begins with a defined question and ends with useful intelligence

00:00:04.835 --> 00:00:06.315
for an authorized audience.

00:00:06.315 --> 00:00:10.225
The requirement establishes purpose, scope, constraints, and stopping conditions.

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:13.900
The collection plan turns those boundaries into prioritized source activities.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.220
Collection records URLs, timestamps, context,

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:20.395
and approved preservation artifacts while respecting access controls and privacy.

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:23.250
Processing deduplicates, tags, organizes timelines,

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.795
and maps relationships without losing provenance.

00:00:25.795 --> 00:00:29.515
Facts, claims, assumptions, and judgments remain visibly separate.

00:00:29.515 --> 00:00:33.570
Validation examines origin, timeliness, bias, manipulation, and source independence.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:38.235
Corroboration relies on genuinely separate evidence, not repeated copies of one claim.

00:00:38.235 --> 00:00:42.620
Analysis tests competing explanations, identifies gaps, avoids confirmation bias,

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.376
and documents reasoning.

00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:47.715
Reporting answers the requirement with evidence references, calibrated confidence,

00:00:47.715 --> 00:00:49.915
limitations, and proportionate next steps.

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:54.120
Dissemination protects sensitive information, and feedback improves the next cycle.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.780
Ethics, legal authority, privacy, documentation,

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.360
and source reliability are not optional extras.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.265
They are controls embedded throughout the workflow.

00:01:01.265 --> 00:01:05.090
The goal is not maximum collection; it is a defensible answer produced through scoped,

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.680
lawful, repeatable, and responsible intelligence work.
